      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This private compatibility module only declares the legacy resource and\n selector address shapes; it has no handwritten executable code. Its derived\n serialization and identity operations do not emit source-line measurements.\n The source-tool argument and delivery regressions in `agent/tests.rs`\n exercise these addresses through the legacy adapter. Supported path-based\n address construction is tested separately in `tests/outline_content.rs`."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/resource.rs` is acceptable.\n\n- **Source matches the stated reason.** The file holds only two plain data declarations, `struct[ResourceId]` and `struct[OutlineId]`. Both derive `Clone`, `Debug`, `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `Serialize` and `Deserialize`. Neither has a handwritten function body, so there is no executable code of its own to measure. The commentary says this, and the file agrees. A file-level exception for the 80% instrumented-line threshold is the right scope.\n- **The cited tests exist and exercise the types.**\n  - The commentary says the legacy addresses are exercised in `agent/tests.rs`. That holds. `source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results` and the other source-tool tests build `ResourceId` and `OutlineId` values. `agent/sources.rs#impl[SourceSession<'_, P, F>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[dispatch]` deserializes a `ResourceId` and constructs an `OutlineId`.\n  - The commentary says path-based address construction is tested in `tests/outline_content.rs`. That also holds. `addresses_reconstruct_without_reading_the_file` and `selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits` use `OutlineData::new` and `OutlineData::root`.\n- **The reason is substantive.** It says the module has no executable code and that its derived operations emit no line measurements. It does not rest on difficulty alone.\n- **The citation is allowed here.** It sits on a source file's root item, which is a permitted use of this built-in.",
